+# Shared Alerts functional acceptance — current source
+
+Current assigned baseline: `0111dfdb58c22ba7149f5a499a15682505aba797`, branch `codex/shared-functional-acceptance-20261119`. This is the controlling current-source inventory and controller handoff, not an execution result. Coordinator owns integration, commits and hosted runtime admission. No production release is authorized by this work.
+
+## Status and evidence boundaries
+
+The earlier a8/957 image passed both Harbor/Northstar navigation, cold hidden unread, hydrated hidden unread and one actual TradersLink Tests Discord delivery. Those results used genuine sessions with SyntheticAgreement communities and an in-memory queue. They do not prove current-image behavior, canonical native SQL delivery, genuine two-guild ownership or full feature acceptance. Frozen601 tooling and its reviews remain historical and must not be relabeled for0111.
+
+Current0111 browser/provider execution: **UNRUN**. Twelve isolated native database cases PASS; they do not close the browser/provider requirements. The previous private runtime binding still names a8/957; Coordinator is independently qualifying the new image. No capability has been minted or old binding repinned here. Coordinator supplied fresh authenticated destination metadata; its exact scope is recorded below. Native owners/publishers/reviewers and current case admission remain separate prerequisites. This record supersedes the old preparation's Website-only positive assumption.
+
+Community owns canonical finite-controller, destination guards, `shared-alerts-delivery.ts`, parts cancellation and source dispatch selection changes. Shared owns this inventory, selector/result requirements and isolated feature findings/tests. Do not duplicate Community edits or change normal background behavior to satisfy a test.
+
+Dependencies: ignored local symlink to Coordinator-approved `/home/traderlink/projects/community-combined-production-review-20261117/node_modules`. Lock SHA256 `4cefe56a3899db538c7adec0956fb7236664c78009d5c78c824a12c869357bcb`; installed required entries match,116 optional platform entries absent. Next16.2.6, Vitest4.1.4, TypeScript5.9.3, better-sqlite3 12.9.0. No copy or installation; generated outputs must remain private to this lane/run.
+
+## Current source facts controlling cases
+
+- Normal `captureSharedAlertPublication` requires both `TRADERLINK_SHARED_ALERTS_DELIVERY_ENABLED === '1'` and the actual normal publication distribution `discord`. Website-only is a negative: zero source Discord jobs and zero Shared jobs. Canonical positive cases select and budget BOTH real source publication deliveries and receiver Shared parts. A test must not invent distribution rows or globally start workers.
+- Actual Shared SQL IDs can be32 lowercase hexadecimal characters from `randomblob(16)`. Preserve them verbatim; a UUIDv4-only validator is incompatible. Correction/withdrawal `event_key` is distinct from `delivery_id`.
+- `runAvailable(1)` on the baseline is NOT an exact-job fence: interrupted reconciliation, original-followup cancellation and stopped-parts cancellation can change unrelated rows before, inside and after the selected loop. Finite execution needs explicit selected IDs for all those writes, including nested failure paths. A transport allowlist alone is insufficient.
+- Shared correction/withdrawal currently makes a labelled followup POST referencing the confirmed original. Verify that actual behavior and the explicitly preserved original. Source common publishing has its own revision/PATCH/DELETE semantics; do not claim those from a Shared followup receipt.
+- Multipart rows are created lazily during a successful parent claim. Their key is `(delivery_id,content_revision,part_number)` with stable nonce and frozen body. Never regenerate or resend a confirmed part. A successful part resets the parent attempt count while each part retains its own cap.
+- An unknown network/5xx outcome holds the relevant part/job as uncertain.429 persists cooldown, including a genuine bot-global cooldown. Do not erase or shorten a real cooldown during cleanup or assert unrelated-metadata invariance across a legitimate global cooldown change.
